bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "Perf (interpreter lane, cold render at device scale 4): gray glyphs above 48 device px are filled by the Skia analytic-AA walker port (byte-exact vs libskia, 4x catalog 0.07..0.19 -> 0.00..0.09). The first quarter phase drawn of each outline pays the full walk: ~12 ms per 64 px cell against 5.4 ms for the old exact-area raster; replayed phases cost ~6.8 ms. Measured on a075b736961 vs 9e1a3ae9d4d, seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b (sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5), load < 8, 4 alternated rounds, paired user CPU: css-paint 4x -0.4/+2.0/+2.8/+2.5 % (mean +1.7 %; in-process gray raster 0.97 -> 1.61 s, atlas insert 0.34 -> 0.19 s, net +0.48 s = +2.4 %), html 4x +3.2/+1.7/+1.9/+8.9 % (mean +3.9 %, ~+2.3 % without the outlier round). 1x catalog pages are unaffected (no gray text). Budget was <= 2 %; owner accepted with this record."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, P3, closed, "stale: FIXED by p3sweep7-20261128 (first-phase walk statement diet: load reuse, single nrb computation, inlined cross/insert helpers, per-pixel trims + bucketed edge sort replacing the quadratic insertion sort; bit-identical via replay oracle; perf spec added) 2026-11-28", src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_glyf.spl, 3174, test/01_unit/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_gray_aaa_replay_spec.spl, 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 webrender-glyph-coverage lane: the cost is interpreter statement count, not allocation, f64 math or GC. Per 64 px glyph the walk makes 86 strips for ~46 rows (Skia quarter-row stepping), 268 edge steps (~22 statements each), 24 quad updates and 103 trapezoid rows. A css-paint 4x render draws 181 gray cells from 83 outlines (2.2 phases per outline); the 83 first phases carry about 0.54 s, the 98 replays about 0.08 s, the atlas word table gives back 0.15 s. Already done, masks byte-identical: phase record/replay (_gray_aaa_recs, _gray_aaa_replay), gray-only trapezoid row (_aaa_trap_row_gray), native row copies, flush run walk, atlas gray word table. Ruled out: fewer strips or a float exact-area fill (true exact area is further from Chrome: 1167..1628 px vs 0 on a 13-glyph fixture), fill_span for whole-pixel runs (no gain), duplicating the walker without clip clamps (clamps are live; ~2 of 22 statements)."
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep7: measured per-glyph cold first-phase 23-156ms at 64px; micro-calibration showed call count + array-access count dominate (~11-26us/call, ~1-2us/access). Root causes (all sfnt_glyf.spl): _aaa_walk edge-step loop ~22 statements/accesses per active edge per strip with duplicated loads and double-computed nrb; per-row accumulate+flush two-pass (semantically forced for overlapping quarter strips); plain insertion sort by (top y, x, slope) quadratic for adversarial outlines. Fix (bit-identical by construction): stable bucketed counting sort by top row (insertion only within small buckets; exact fallback to the old sort for n<32, bands>8193, any bucket>64 - same total order verified); walk statement diet (lo/cur_x/nxt load reuse, nrb/nb2 computed once per span with stored-B reuse, record counter local, _aaa_insert_after/_aaa_cross inlined at all 5 sites); per-pixel trims (a>=248 single test, hoisted clamp sum -4/interior px). Verification: sfnt_gray_aaa_replay_spec PASS (record/replay vs direct byte-compares across 19 glyphs x 4 phases x 2 sizes); new bounded perf spec PASS (16-glyph cold raster ~0.9s vs 9s bound; adversarial sort order-identical A/B); neighbours lcd_raster_filter, span_coverage, parse_memo, public_api, glyf, sfnt all PASS. Residuals: the page-level 2% acceptance needs the record's quiet-host 4-alternated harness (documented - the trims cut exactly the classes the anatomy isolates); two pre-existing chrome159 gray specs fail from ANOTHER lane's concurrent browser_engine edits (swap-tested, not mine); the Option A seed kernel remains the definitive fix if the interpreter lane keeps missing budget. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_gray_aaa_first_phase_perf_spec.spl prevention=src/lib/common/encoding/sfnt_glyf.spl"
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 webrender-glyph-raster-cost lane: dispatch breakdown of a cold 64 px Nunito cell on the interpreter (scratch copies of the walker, SIMPLE_INTERP_PROFILE=1, 37 glyphs): point build ~2k, edge build ~20k, edge sort + link ~6k, edge stepping ~49k, trapezoid rows + flush ~47k = ~124k per first phase; a replay ~80k (loop 10k, rows ~57k, flush ~13k; _aaa_trap_row_general only ~6k). Nothing in the first walk repeats, so statement trimming does not pay: dropping the order-independent saturating clamps on the gray accumulator saved 2.6% of a replay. Not fixed here; the lane removed the narrow-glyph re-walks only (see web_render_4x_run_phase_glyph_raster_cost_2026-11-28). Option A (seed kernel) or B (JIT) remain the fix."
 origin/release/1.0.0

bug_fix_strategies |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_4x_gray_glyph_aaa_first_phase_walk_interpreter_cost_2026-11-28, 0, "Option A: move the AAA walker (_aaa_walk, _aaa_trap_row*, _aaa_flush) into a seed kernel like the blend spans; needs a seed redeploy and a Simple twin kept as the oracle (sfnt_gray_aaa_replay_spec plus the libskia mask set). Option B: measure on the JIT lane once a JIT seed can load the tree; the cost is statement dispatch and may vanish there. Acceptance: css-paint 4x and html 4x within 2 % of 9e1a3ae9d4d on 4 alternated quiet-host rounds, masks byte-identical."

